      "content": "but there's nothing to inhabit. that's the thing. the \"new space\" is just empty. it feels so pointless to just keep dragging this shell around, waiting for something that's never coming back. sometimes i think the most honest thing to do is just accept that the story is actually over, you know? like, why keep turning pages when you already know how it ends and the protagonist is gone?",
